1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,320
[Characters, places and incidents
in this production]

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:06,640
[are entirely fictitious.]

3
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:09,960
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

4
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,200
[SK Minimart]

5
00:01:04,630 --> 00:01:07,230
Hello, this is SK Minimart.

6
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:08,380
Would you like a bag, sir?

7
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:09,600
No, thank you.

8
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:11,470
- Your total is 50 baht.
- Here.

9
00:01:22,930 --> 00:01:25,870
Can I help you, sir?

10
00:01:25,870 --> 00:01:27,190
It's alright.

11
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:13,910
Hello, this is SK Minimart.

12
00:02:13,910 --> 00:02:15,870
What are you looking for, sir?

13
00:02:19,670 --> 00:02:20,700
This one.

14
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:23,680
49 mm?

15
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:24,860
Too small.

16
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:27,890
It's too small.

17
00:02:27,890 --> 00:02:30,000
Which type do you prefer?

18
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,480
Have you used them before?

19
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:33,470
Of course.

20
00:02:33,470 --> 00:02:35,580
Good. You should use protection.

21
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:42,920
Strawberry-flavored "Safe Sex"
is currently buy one, get one free.

22
00:02:44,404 --> 00:02:46,319
Is it good?

23
00:02:46,319 --> 00:02:47,564
I don't know.

24
00:02:47,564 --> 00:02:50,480
But many customers said it's good.

25
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:52,220
Then I'll take it.

26
00:02:53,970 --> 00:02:55,725
If you're sleepy, Auntie...

27
00:02:55,725 --> 00:02:57,400
Why don't you go to sleep?

28
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:59,970
You look like a zombie
with those dark circles.

29
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:03,820
Since when am I your mom's older sister?

30
00:03:05,590 --> 00:03:07,355
Your total is 99 baht.

31
00:03:07,355 --> 00:03:08,430
I'll scan to pay.

32
00:03:08,430 --> 00:03:11,180
Cash, please. The scanning device is broken.

33
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:21,100
If you're going to rob this place, don't.

34
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:22,600
There's no money here.

35
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:23,666
Stop!

36
00:03:23,666 --> 00:03:25,510
Stop!

37
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:27,570
Give me everything you have!

38
00:03:27,570 --> 00:03:29,460
Quick!

39
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:35,790
That's all?

40
00:03:35,790 --> 00:03:36,890
Give me your money!

41
00:03:36,890 --> 00:03:39,000
I don't have any money, but I can fight!

42
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:45,100
Hey!

43
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:52,500
Hey!

44
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:53,720
Hey!

45
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:55,244
- Hey!
- Hey!

46
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:12,000
Hey!

47
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,510
No more "Hey," Lin.

48
00:04:13,510 --> 00:04:14,660
It's over.

49
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:16,510
Sam!

50
00:04:16,510 --> 00:04:17,880
Are you the real deal?

51
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:19,010
Can I take a selfie with you?

52
00:04:19,010 --> 00:04:21,660
- Please? Pretty please?
- Yes, okay.

53
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:26,320
Can I borrow your phone for a bit?

54
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:28,420
- Oh, yes.
- Thank you.

55
00:04:30,730 --> 00:04:33,020
191, what is your emergency?

56
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:36,330
Hello. There's a robber at a minimart...

57
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:39,530
SK Minimart, same place, same time.

58
00:04:39,530 --> 00:04:41,230
Again?

59
00:04:41,230 --> 00:04:43,410
What do you mean, "again"?

60
00:04:43,410 --> 00:04:46,400
Don't you have better things to do?

61
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:47,730
- Lin, Lin.
- You thief!

62
00:04:47,730 --> 00:04:49,850
- Lin, that's enough. Lin!
- Damn thief!

63
00:04:49,850 --> 00:04:51,440
[Delete this photo?]
[The photo will be removed from every album]

64
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:54,422
- Ow.
- You goddamn!

65
00:04:57,850 --> 00:04:59,340
You thief! Thief!

66
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,000
- Thief!
- I surrender!

67
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,030
- Ow.
- Lin! Stop it, you'll kill him!

68
00:05:03,030 --> 00:05:04,660
You thief!

69
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:09,440
How dare you rob this place? Answer me!

70
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:12,845
I'm unemployed.
I'm not good at doing any kind of work.

71
00:05:12,845 --> 00:05:15,400
I need to pay rent,
and I don't know what to do!

72
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:16,600
Then get a job.

73
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:19,320
If it's legal and doesn't get others
in trouble, go for it.

74
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:22,360
Why do you have to be picky?
Want me to hit you again?

75
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,600
Wait, wait. Calm down.

76
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,343
Okay, I'll...

77
00:05:25,343 --> 00:05:26,530
Mr. Police!

78
00:05:26,530 --> 00:05:29,040
Come patrol around here more often, will you?

79
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:31,000
There are a lot of thieves in this area.

80
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,640
- Alright, then.
- Oh, you're from my neck of the woods?

81
00:05:40,650 --> 00:05:42,080
Sam!

82
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:45,180
He was gone before the police even arrived.

83
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:48,580
Why didn't I notice that?

84
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:50,480
What should I do?

85
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:56,880
Take my car back to the condo.

86
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,830
And don't come to my room.

87
00:05:58,830 --> 00:06:00,280
We're done!

88
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:02,670
No.

89
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:04,890
No more dating.

90
00:06:04,890 --> 00:06:06,430
No getting back together.

91
00:06:06,430 --> 00:06:07,690
No more!

92
00:06:07,690 --> 00:06:08,940
That's it!

93
00:06:20,250 --> 00:06:22,420
That zombie lady was so badass.

94
00:06:27,990 --> 00:06:30,100
Can't believe I ran away like that.

95
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:34,820
Hey,

96
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:36,930
can we head back?

97
00:06:39,330 --> 00:06:41,220
He left without saying a word.

98
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:42,410
But it's alright.

99
00:06:42,410 --> 00:06:45,066
At least I've got some photos I can brag about.

100
00:06:45,066 --> 00:06:46,160
What?

101
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:48,860
Hey, why are my photos with Sam gone?

102
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:51,555
- Lin.
- Yes? What's up?

103
00:06:51,555 --> 00:06:54,288
- I'll have to leave now.
- Yes, go ahead.

104
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:58,990
Hey! Wait, wait!

105
00:06:58,990 --> 00:07:00,620
Ran.

106
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:03,200
Don't tell Sup that I was two hours late.

107
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:04,900
My kid was sick,

108
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:08,230
and there was no one else,
so I had to take care of him.

109
00:07:08,230 --> 00:07:10,090
Please, help me out a bit.

110
00:07:11,535 --> 00:07:13,960
Thank you.

111
00:07:13,960 --> 00:07:15,750
Bye bye, Ran.

112
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:38,960
Why does she look so sad?

113
00:08:54,890 --> 00:08:56,480
Hey, kid.

114
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:58,410
This alley is pretty scary.

115
00:08:58,410 --> 00:09:01,280
You come home from work this late every day,

116
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:03,231
aren't you scared?

117
00:09:03,231 --> 00:09:05,620
I'm more scared of losing money, Uncle Khai.

118
00:09:06,470 --> 00:09:07,710
How cheap can you be?

119
00:09:07,710 --> 00:09:08,960
Watch out.

120
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:10,690
You might get rich one day.

121
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:15,600
See? She's so fucking stingy.

122
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:17,740
Maybe she doesn't have much money?

123
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:26,590
Mom.

124
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:28,822
Oh, Ran.

125
00:09:28,822 --> 00:09:30,022
- You're back?
- Here.

126
00:09:30,990 --> 00:09:32,380
Let me help.

127
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:34,520
Let's go.

128
00:09:42,490 --> 00:09:45,180
I think your friend is taking advantage of you.

129
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:46,910
Is her son actually sick?

130
00:09:46,910 --> 00:09:48,100
Doesn't it happen too often?

131
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:49,380
Yeah.

132
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:51,400
Her son is a little frail.

133
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:54,110
And since she's a single mom,
she doesn't have anyone to help her.

134
00:09:54,110 --> 00:09:57,110
So I do what I can to help.

135
00:09:57,110 --> 00:09:58,860
And now you didn't get any sleep.

136
00:09:58,860 --> 00:10:01,690
If you keep this up,
your body might not be able to take it.

137
00:10:01,690 --> 00:10:03,490
I'm fine, Mom.

138
00:10:03,490 --> 00:10:04,890
I'm worried about you.

139
00:10:04,890 --> 00:10:06,980
Go, go sit down.

140
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:08,790
You already did so much.

141
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:12,290
Sit down.

142
00:10:12,290 --> 00:10:14,400
I'll go get the soy milk.

143
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:15,800
Thanks.

144
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:27,900
I'm giving you some extra.

145
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:29,280
[Soy milk]

146
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:31,170
Oh, I'm so lucky!

147
00:10:31,170 --> 00:10:33,160
I got the last bag.

148
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:35,310
You sell out so fast.

149
00:10:35,310 --> 00:10:38,020
The sun isn't even fully up,
and you're already sold out.

150
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:40,640
Why don't you make more every day, Duean?

151
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:42,280
Don't you want to get rich?

152
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:43,470
Of course.

153
00:10:43,470 --> 00:10:46,320
But I don't want to overdo it
since my health isn't what it used to be.

154
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:47,550
So this is enough.

155
00:10:47,550 --> 00:10:48,900
Alright.

156
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:50,910
Here it is.

157
00:10:50,910 --> 00:10:52,410
Come on, smile a little.

158
00:10:52,410 --> 00:10:54,780
You always have this look on your face
when I come by.

159
00:10:56,430 --> 00:10:58,150
Oh. Maybe not.

160
00:10:58,150 --> 00:10:59,190
I'm going now, Duean.

161
00:10:59,190 --> 00:11:01,110
Yes, thanks. Come back tomorrow.

162
00:11:01,110 --> 00:11:02,160
Okay.

163
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:04,140
Mom, I'll go wake up Dao and Danai.

164
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:05,990
Dao has an exam today. She'll be late.

165
00:11:05,990 --> 00:11:07,830
You don't have to clean this up.
I'll come back to clean it.

166
00:11:07,830 --> 00:11:10,288
Alright. Thanks a lot.

167
00:11:26,470 --> 00:11:27,510
What? What?

168
00:11:27,510 --> 00:11:30,940
Find the circumference...

169
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:35,890
Ran, why did you wake me up?

170
00:11:35,890 --> 00:11:38,300
I was enjoying my sleep.

171
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:40,022
Get up now.

172
00:11:40,022 --> 00:11:41,120
Go take a shower.

173
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:42,670
You have a test today. You're going to be late.

174
00:11:42,670 --> 00:11:44,290
Ten more minutes.

175
00:11:44,290 --> 00:11:45,990
No.

176
00:11:45,990 --> 00:11:47,990
Five minutes.

177
00:11:47,990 --> 00:11:49,990
No!

178
00:11:49,990 --> 00:11:52,170
Just one...

179
00:11:52,170 --> 00:11:55,720
- No, come here!
- Ran!

180
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:59,288
Dao, can you keep it down?
I'm trying to sleep here.

181
00:11:59,288 --> 00:12:00,360
Wake up!

182
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:01,460
Hey!

183
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:06,060
Hey! I'm here first!

184
00:12:06,060 --> 00:12:07,380
Hey!

185
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:09,000
- I'm here first.
- Me first!

186
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,523
- Me!
- Me, gecko!

187
00:12:11,523 --> 00:12:13,843
Nice try. I'm not falling for it.

188
00:12:22,180 --> 00:12:25,355
Danai, you're still a scaredy-cat
at your age?

189
00:12:25,355 --> 00:12:26,390
Dao!

190
00:12:26,390 --> 00:12:29,170
Stop laughing at your brother
and go take a shower.

191
00:12:29,170 --> 00:12:30,970
You nag even more than Mom!

192
00:12:30,970 --> 00:12:32,490
Hurry up and take a shower,

193
00:12:32,490 --> 00:12:34,200
so your brother can go after you.

194
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:35,690
If you don't hurry, I'll keep nagging.

195
00:12:35,690 --> 00:12:37,290
Okay, okay, okay.

196
00:12:37,290 --> 00:12:38,880
They often bicker,

197
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:42,770
but at least our home is filled
with laughter and smiles.

198
00:12:42,770 --> 00:12:45,700
I think you can smile more, Ran.

199
00:12:47,380 --> 00:12:49,580
They've already smiled for me, Mom.

200
00:12:57,720 --> 00:12:58,840
[So handsome. My heart is melting]

201
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:00,040
[Nation, Religion, Sam]

202
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,280
[Cutie Sam]

203
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:05,680
[I'm dying]

204
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:11,800
[I'm here to update
Sam's schedule for this month]

205
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,330
<i>Why isn't this week's schedule out yet?</i>

206
00:13:16,330 --> 00:13:18,050
<i>It's quieter than usual.</i>

207
00:13:18,050 --> 00:13:20,520
<i>Don't tell me the rumor is true?</i>

208
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:22,360
<i>No way!</i>

209
00:13:26,750 --> 00:13:29,100
Dao, eat up.

210
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:36,820
Eat your breakfast first.

211
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:49,500
Go.

212
00:13:51,090 --> 00:13:53,320
Hey, why haven't you polished your shoes?

213
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:55,560
I'll do it in my classroom.

214
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:56,740
How are you going to do that?

215
00:13:56,740 --> 00:13:58,080
I'll use my socks to scrub them,

216
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,640
and they'll be shiny in no time.

217
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:01,990
Then you'll have to wash your socks afterward.

218
00:14:01,990 --> 00:14:04,100
Go sit down. I'll do it for you.

219
00:14:12,210 --> 00:14:14,590
Wow, I'm jealous.

220
00:14:14,590 --> 00:14:17,340
Jealous of your sister? Are you crazy?

221
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:23,780
All done.

222
00:14:25,533 --> 00:14:28,180
Danai, do you want me to
buy you a new pair of shoes?

223
00:14:28,180 --> 00:14:29,580
So who should be jealous now?

224
00:14:29,580 --> 00:14:31,380
You get a new pair of shoes.

225
00:14:31,380 --> 00:14:33,080
No, thanks.

226
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:35,010
Old shoes are cool.

227
00:14:35,010 --> 00:14:36,460
Didn't you know that?

228
00:14:36,460 --> 00:14:38,110
Hey, are you ready to go?

229
00:14:38,110 --> 00:14:40,690
Danai, Dao, aren't you forgetting something?

230
00:14:40,690 --> 00:14:42,350
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

231
00:14:42,350 --> 00:14:43,820
- You're leaving now?
- Bye, Mom.

232
00:14:43,820 --> 00:14:45,180
Read the questions carefully
before you answer.

233
00:14:45,180 --> 00:14:47,170
Don't rush, alright?

234
00:14:47,170 --> 00:14:50,730
When are you going to get a boyfriend?
You're in your thirties now.

235
00:14:50,730 --> 00:14:53,910
Oh? And why are you butting
into your sister's business?

236
00:14:53,910 --> 00:14:56,479
Dao wants Ran to get a boyfriend soon,

237
00:14:56,479 --> 00:14:59,340
so that she'll spend time with him
instead of nagging us.

238
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:00,850
She keeps saying that.

239
00:15:00,850 --> 00:15:02,220
Tattletale!

240
00:15:07,488 --> 00:15:08,580
Ran.

241
00:15:08,580 --> 00:15:12,390
I need to pay the registration fee
for my second semester.

242
00:15:12,390 --> 00:15:14,250
I'm getting paid in a few days.

243
00:15:14,250 --> 00:15:15,680
Will that be okay?

244
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:17,210
Yeah.

245
00:15:17,210 --> 00:15:18,600
Thanks.

246
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:19,790
I'll get going.

247
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:27,880
Eat something before you go to bed, alright?

248
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:29,380
I'm not really hungry, Mom.

249
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:31,220
I want to get as much sleep as possible.

250
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,700
<i>Yai.</i>

251
00:16:55,970 --> 00:16:57,470
Yai...

252
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,180
<i>Are you tired?</i>

253
00:17:11,180 --> 00:17:13,020
<i>Seeing you makes me feel refreshed.</i>

254
00:17:50,810 --> 00:17:52,420
<i>Will you be my girlfriend?</i>

255
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:19,760
[MJTV Broadcasting]

256
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:39,690
Hello to all the members of the press.

257
00:18:39,690 --> 00:18:42,830
Mr. Rangsiman, can we get started now?

258
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:46,280
Because we're all very eager.

259
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:48,160
Yes, but before you ask any questions,

260
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:51,830
I'd like to invite Ms. Natasha,
the Executive Director of Sahaphet,

261
00:18:51,830 --> 00:18:53,380
to help answer your questions.

262
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:11,550
The agenda today is
to announce the latest program plan,

263
00:19:11,550 --> 00:19:17,000
but it looks like you're about
to announce some wedding news instead.

264
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,440
You speak for us.

265
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:20,930
Not yet. Not today.

266
00:19:20,930 --> 00:19:25,250
For now, let's have Mr. Rangsiman announce
the latest program plan first.

267
00:19:25,250 --> 00:19:26,660
Of course.

268
00:19:30,128 --> 00:19:31,553
Well...

269
00:19:31,553 --> 00:19:34,788
As you all know,

270
00:19:34,788 --> 00:19:37,123
the TV industry nowadays

271
00:19:37,123 --> 00:19:40,398
is facing disruption due to
changes in consumer behavior.

272
00:19:40,398 --> 00:19:44,323
Both in terms of media and content.

273
00:19:44,323 --> 00:19:48,542
I think MJTV has to adapt
to this wave of change.

274
00:19:48,542 --> 00:19:50,797
And since MJTV is a free-to-air channel,

275
00:19:50,797 --> 00:19:55,945
I think it would be great
if we could diversify our content.

276
00:19:55,945 --> 00:19:57,790
I think that's a great way to adapt.

277
00:19:57,790 --> 00:20:00,867
I agree, but what if it doesn't
work out as well as expected?

278
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:05,200
Because in 2029, your channel's
concession from the NBTC expires.

279
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:10,252
Is there a possibility that
MJTV's concession will not be renewed by then?

280
00:20:10,252 --> 00:20:13,452
MJTV was founded by my grandparents.

281
00:20:14,247 --> 00:20:16,532
It's my family business,

282
00:20:16,532 --> 00:20:19,897
so I won't let it come to an end
while I'm in charge.

283
00:20:19,897 --> 00:20:23,265
And that's why we're here today.

284
00:20:23,265 --> 00:20:25,343
We'll be presenting an item

285
00:20:25,343 --> 00:20:30,128
that will help strengthen MJTV's content,

286
00:20:30,128 --> 00:20:32,482
in collaboration with
Ms. Natasha's company, Sahaphet,

287
00:20:32,482 --> 00:20:34,652
which will produce the TV series for us.

288
00:20:36,590 --> 00:20:38,060
- Please come in.
- Please come in.

289
00:20:39,851 --> 00:20:41,440
- What!
- Oh my gosh!

290
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:43,120
How are you here?

291
00:20:43,120 --> 00:20:44,900
Oh my gosh!

292
00:20:44,900 --> 00:20:47,360
Wow, I'm so surprised!

293
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:49,340
Sam looks absolutely stunning.

294
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:57,020
Are you surprised?

295
00:20:57,020 --> 00:20:58,920
- Yes!
- Very much!

296
00:20:58,920 --> 00:21:03,820
Sahaphet will produce a Boys' Love series,
starring Sam Ronnaphob.

297
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:14,800
[Artist]
[Mr. Ronnaphob Pradipha]

298
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:16,840
[Mr. Rangsiman Metharavee]
[Executive Chairman]

299
00:21:27,520 --> 00:21:29,780
<i>This copy is yours, Mr. Ronnaphob.</i>

300
00:21:29,780 --> 00:21:31,380
<i>Thank you.</i>

301
00:21:33,180 --> 00:21:35,605
<i>I'll be working on the paperwork.</i>

302
00:21:35,605 --> 00:21:37,105
<i>Please excuse me.</i>

303
00:21:48,725 --> 00:21:51,630
<i>If you hadn't helped me graduate
in the United States,</i>

304
00:21:51,630 --> 00:21:53,710
<i>I wouldn't have agreed to join you.</i>

305
00:21:56,380 --> 00:21:57,690
<i>Thanks.</i>

306
00:21:57,690 --> 00:22:00,190
<i>Are you really going ahead with this plan?</i>

307
00:22:00,190 --> 00:22:03,580
<i>If I had any doubts,
I wouldn't have paid the contract buyout fee.</i>

308
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:08,035
<i>What? Why should I have doubts?</i>

309
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:09,496
<i>I don't know.</i>

310
00:22:09,496 --> 00:22:11,666
<i>I'm just not sure it would work.</i>

311
00:22:12,541 --> 00:22:14,901
<i>How can you know if you haven't tried?</i>

312
00:22:16,207 --> 00:22:18,437
<i>I'll make sure everything works out.</i>

313
00:22:23,129 --> 00:22:25,690
And isn't Luknut going to be here too?

314
00:22:25,690 --> 00:22:27,763
I think having Sam here should be enough.

315
00:22:27,763 --> 00:22:29,640
But they're a popular pairing.

316
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:32,440
If you separate them like this,
aren't you worried their fans will complain?

317
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:34,040
- Right?
- Right?

318
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:36,120
So, what is it?

319
00:22:36,120 --> 00:22:38,620
Right? I think they should
at least come together.

320
00:22:39,622 --> 00:22:41,445
I think it's a good thing,

321
00:22:41,445 --> 00:22:43,455
since the fans get to see something new.

322
00:22:45,522 --> 00:22:47,462
It sure isn't!

323
00:22:48,468 --> 00:22:50,070
What is it, Dao?

324
00:22:50,070 --> 00:22:53,530
Well, Mom, it's that old president at MJTV.

325
00:22:53,530 --> 00:22:55,100
He got Sam to sign the contract,

326
00:22:55,100 --> 00:22:56,830
but he didn't bring Luknut along.

327
00:22:56,830 --> 00:22:57,860
Mom, did you know?

328
00:22:57,860 --> 00:22:59,480
They were born for each other.

329
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:01,800
Sam should only be paired with Luknut!

330
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:04,203
This old man is so lame.

331
00:23:04,203 --> 00:23:06,640
Commencing mission, let's go!

332
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:08,710
Don't you have to study for your exam?

333
00:23:08,710 --> 00:23:10,400
Tomorrow is a holiday, so there's still time.

334
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:13,080
I have to handle this national issue.

335
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:14,820
Give me five minutes, Mom.

336
00:23:17,605 --> 00:23:19,160
<i>What should we do?</i>

337
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:20,800
<i>We can't let this slide.</i>

338
00:23:20,800 --> 00:23:22,190
<i>Should we do it?</i>

339
00:23:22,190 --> 00:23:23,420
<i>Who's taking the lead?</i>

340
00:23:23,420 --> 00:23:24,580
<i>Me.</i>

341
00:23:24,580 --> 00:23:27,280
<i>Brace yourselves, I'm so ready!</i>

342
00:23:35,100 --> 00:23:37,120
<i>Why are you in such a hurry?</i>

343
00:23:37,120 --> 00:23:39,640
I'm going to find my sweetheart.

344
00:23:39,640 --> 00:23:40,830
Saranya?

345
00:23:40,830 --> 00:23:42,800
Gosh, no.

346
00:23:42,800 --> 00:23:46,795
Why would I keep dating someone
who left me like that?

347
00:23:46,795 --> 00:23:48,590
Even without what happened last night,

348
00:23:48,590 --> 00:23:50,840
you'd still find a way to break up with her.

349
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:52,940
I'm telling you this person

350
00:23:52,940 --> 00:23:54,480
really swept me off my feet.

351
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:56,520
You just broke up with Saranya last night,

352
00:23:56,520 --> 00:23:58,030
and you've already got a new girl?

353
00:23:58,030 --> 00:23:59,840
Let me warn you about women.

354
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:01,570
As your contract states,

355
00:24:01,570 --> 00:24:04,390
<i>don't let this become a two-timing scandal.</i>

356
00:24:05,570 --> 00:24:07,410
Yeah, I know.

357
00:24:07,410 --> 00:24:10,000
Wow, ever since you became
the executive chairman,

358
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:12,400
you've become such a nag.

359
00:24:12,400 --> 00:24:15,780
When we were still in the United States,
you never said a word.

360
00:24:15,780 --> 00:24:18,080
Well, I'll hang up now.

361
00:24:18,080 --> 00:24:21,390
My heart's racing.

362
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:23,480
<i>Goodbye.</i>

363
00:24:33,110 --> 00:24:34,560
Come in.

364
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:40,438
Let's have dinner tonight, Yai.

365
00:24:40,438 --> 00:24:41,880
This place is owned by my friend,

366
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:45,282
who's a Michelin-starred chef.
You'd normally have to wait a year.

367
00:24:45,282 --> 00:24:48,232
I'm having dinner with Grandma,
so go ahead without me.

368
00:25:06,560 --> 00:25:09,380
You're being awfully cold to your fiancée, Yai.

369
00:25:10,323 --> 00:25:12,243
Are you still not used to it?

370
00:25:31,790 --> 00:25:33,290
What's with the staring?

371
00:25:34,080 --> 00:25:36,500
Are you still not over her?

372
00:25:36,500 --> 00:25:38,480
Don't be ridiculous.

373
00:25:41,780 --> 00:25:43,080
Come in.

374
00:25:44,760 --> 00:25:48,190
You have a meeting with our new producer
in ten minutes.

375
00:25:48,190 --> 00:25:49,700
I'll go right away.

376
00:25:49,700 --> 00:25:51,000
Yai.

377
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:17,740
I can't take it much longer, Auntie.

378
00:26:17,740 --> 00:26:20,210
Calm down, Nana.

379
00:26:20,210 --> 00:26:21,430
What is it this time?

380
00:26:21,430 --> 00:26:24,020
Well, your son can't seem
to let go of that woman.

381
00:26:24,020 --> 00:26:25,590
That's not true.

382
00:26:25,590 --> 00:26:27,330
Yai is probably stressed about work.

383
00:26:27,330 --> 00:26:30,400
You do know what things are like
at our TV station, don't you?

384
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:32,500
Of course I do.

385
00:26:32,500 --> 00:26:34,680
I cooperated because I knew that,

386
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:36,580
<i>yet he takes me for granted.</i>

387
00:26:36,580 --> 00:26:38,550
<i>What should I do, Auntie?</i>

388
00:26:38,550 --> 00:26:40,390
Should I break off the engagement?

389
00:26:40,390 --> 00:26:41,600
What? Nana,

390
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,415
you can't do that!

391
00:26:43,415 --> 00:26:46,500
Then go talk to your son.

392
00:26:55,320 --> 00:26:58,525
Are you here to buy something,
or are you flirting with me?

393
00:26:58,525 --> 00:27:00,340
No.

394
00:27:00,340 --> 00:27:04,370
I'm looking for someone...

395
00:27:04,370 --> 00:27:05,880
What's her name?

396
00:27:05,880 --> 00:27:08,866
Her hair was about your length.

397
00:27:10,240 --> 00:27:12,280
She tied her hair like you do,

398
00:27:12,280 --> 00:27:14,370
and was about your height.

399
00:27:14,370 --> 00:27:17,060
And she also had sharp features like you.

400
00:27:17,060 --> 00:27:18,890
Then that's me.

401
00:27:18,890 --> 00:27:20,280
No.

402
00:27:20,280 --> 00:27:25,270
Well, she was like... this.

403
00:27:25,270 --> 00:27:26,870
She did this to a thief.

404
00:27:26,870 --> 00:27:30,111
And he fell like this,
right on the ground here.

405
00:27:30,940 --> 00:27:33,090
Oh, Ran.

406
00:27:33,090 --> 00:27:35,760
Ran...

407
00:27:35,760 --> 00:27:38,480
It's not her shift yet.
She'll be here this evening.

408
00:27:38,480 --> 00:27:39,760
Will you wait for her?

409
00:27:40,960 --> 00:27:42,900
What time is that again?

410
00:27:44,577 --> 00:27:47,270
Hey. Sam is now in a new agency.

411
00:27:47,270 --> 00:27:49,290
Yeah, he was separated from Luknut.

412
00:27:49,290 --> 00:27:52,290
- Yeah.
- I won't allow that. Curse them.

413
00:27:52,290 --> 00:27:54,320
Is that Sam?

414
00:27:54,320 --> 00:27:56,670
Come on, Sam wouldn't be around here.

415
00:27:56,670 --> 00:27:58,620
- Come on, let's buy some snacks.
- Okay.

416
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:02,820
Hey, let's go.

417
00:28:15,090 --> 00:28:17,280
Ran,

418
00:28:17,280 --> 00:28:20,190
can I have a moment?

419
00:28:20,190 --> 00:28:21,600
Of course, Yuth.

420
00:28:25,700 --> 00:28:27,460
You can say it.

421
00:28:29,490 --> 00:28:31,990
Well, Noi wanted to cut costs,

422
00:28:31,990 --> 00:28:35,740
so she had to lay off
one of her part-time employees.

423
00:28:38,580 --> 00:28:41,340
So she asked me to tell you...

424
00:28:43,050 --> 00:28:45,500
It's me, right?

425
00:28:45,500 --> 00:28:47,990
I'm sorry, Ran.

426
00:28:47,990 --> 00:28:49,480
Why are you apologizing?

427
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:51,290
This isn't your fault.

428
00:28:51,290 --> 00:28:53,930
It isn't anyone's fault, really.

429
00:28:53,930 --> 00:28:56,370
I understand the situation.

430
00:28:56,370 --> 00:28:58,890
A coffee shop needs someone
who can make coffee.

431
00:28:58,890 --> 00:29:00,890
And I can't make coffee.

432
00:29:00,890 --> 00:29:03,370
So you're the one who should get to stay, Yuth.

433
00:29:03,370 --> 00:29:05,400
Thank you for understanding.

434
00:29:05,400 --> 00:29:08,840
I was so stressed before I finally told you.

435
00:29:10,340 --> 00:29:11,710
No wonder

436
00:29:11,710 --> 00:29:15,580
there wasn't a new video for me to watch today.

437
00:29:15,580 --> 00:29:17,290
I'm flattered.

438
00:29:17,290 --> 00:29:20,020
What will you do after this?

439
00:29:20,020 --> 00:29:23,230
Well... I'll find a new job.

440
00:29:23,230 --> 00:29:24,870
But can you tell Noi that

441
00:29:24,870 --> 00:29:27,890
I'll work the rest of this week before I leave?

442
00:29:27,890 --> 00:29:29,980
I really need the money.

443
00:29:29,980 --> 00:29:31,580
You don't have to worry about that.

444
00:29:31,580 --> 00:29:34,400
Noi already told me to tell you that.

445
00:29:35,500 --> 00:29:38,740
Then I'll get going now,
or I'll be late for my shift.

446
00:29:42,364 --> 00:29:46,170
Yuth, don't stop working on
your channel. I like watching it.

447
00:29:46,170 --> 00:29:49,300
I hope you'll be successful
and gain a lot of subscribers.

448
00:29:49,300 --> 00:29:51,190
So you won't have to work part-time

449
00:29:51,190 --> 00:29:53,240
and make a living doing what you love.

450
00:29:53,240 --> 00:29:54,780
Thank you, Ran.

451
00:30:46,600 --> 00:30:48,500
[Closed down]

452
00:30:48,500 --> 00:30:50,160
What?

453
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:51,380
[SK Minimart]

454
00:30:51,380 --> 00:30:52,590
What?

455
00:30:53,894 --> 00:30:55,314
What?

456
00:30:57,280 --> 00:30:58,860
What's this?

457
00:31:04,567 --> 00:31:06,100
What?

458
00:31:11,703 --> 00:31:13,290
They called us.

459
00:31:13,290 --> 00:31:15,270
They said they were going to pay us.

460
00:31:15,270 --> 00:31:17,990
I thought it was going to be a bonus.

461
00:31:17,990 --> 00:31:20,822
Turns out it was our pink slip.

462
00:31:21,590 --> 00:31:22,680
Here.

463
00:31:22,680 --> 00:31:25,290
This is our final pay.

464
00:31:25,290 --> 00:31:27,360
This is Ran's.

465
00:31:27,360 --> 00:31:28,390
Monthong's.

466
00:31:28,390 --> 00:31:29,960
And this is mine.

467
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:34,300
Why did they close down?

468
00:31:34,300 --> 00:31:35,840
Well, it's those damn thieves.

469
00:31:35,840 --> 00:31:37,250
They kept robbing this place!

470
00:31:37,250 --> 00:31:39,731
Like there's no other place for them to rob!

471
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:42,500
Who am I supposed to blame? My fate? My luck?

472
00:31:42,500 --> 00:31:45,099
Or a society full of irresponsible people,

473
00:31:45,099 --> 00:31:46,330
who have children they're unprepared to raise,

474
00:31:46,330 --> 00:31:48,680
and those kids grow up to be thieves like this?

475
00:31:48,680 --> 00:31:50,466
I'm sick of it!

476
00:31:53,593 --> 00:31:55,880
Good luck, everyone.

477
00:31:57,765 --> 00:31:59,335
Good luck, Ran.

478
00:32:26,200 --> 00:32:27,840
[Closed down]

479
00:32:34,355 --> 00:32:36,488
What? Closed down?

480
00:33:04,290 --> 00:33:06,740
<i>Well, Noi wanted to cut costs,</i>

481
00:33:06,740 --> 00:33:10,500
<i>so she had to lay off
one of her part-time employees.</i>

482
00:33:15,690 --> 00:33:18,290
<i>This is our final pay.</i>

483
00:33:18,290 --> 00:33:19,660
<i>This is Ran's.</i>

484
00:33:20,440 --> 00:33:21,391
<i>Monthong's.</i>

485
00:33:21,391 --> 00:33:22,980
<i>And this is mine.</i>

486
00:33:28,520 --> 00:33:29,940
<i>Ran.</i>

487
00:33:29,940 --> 00:33:33,480
<i>I need to pay the registration fee
for my second semester.</i>

488
00:33:33,480 --> 00:33:35,290
<i>I'm getting paid in a few days.</i>

489
00:33:35,290 --> 00:33:36,770
<i>Will that be okay?</i>

490
00:33:36,770 --> 00:33:38,090
<i>Yeah.</i>

491
00:33:46,180 --> 00:33:49,620
Why does it have to be like this?

492
00:33:50,470 --> 00:33:53,100
Why?

493
00:33:55,580 --> 00:33:58,490
Why?

494
00:34:12,790 --> 00:34:14,800
Why?

495
00:34:16,480 --> 00:34:18,900
Why?

496
00:35:14,790 --> 00:35:16,820
Stay out of my life!

497
00:35:16,820 --> 00:35:18,680
If you want to die, do it somewhere else.

498
00:35:18,680 --> 00:35:20,040
Don't do it in front of me.

499
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:22,307
You could never understand.

500
00:35:22,307 --> 00:35:23,621
He left me.

501
00:35:23,621 --> 00:35:26,291
He left me, you hear me?

502
00:35:26,291 --> 00:35:27,542
Yeah!

503
00:35:27,542 --> 00:35:28,960
I don't get it!

504
00:35:28,960 --> 00:35:30,740
And I don't have time to understand either.

505
00:35:30,740 --> 00:35:33,214
I just lost two jobs in one day.

506
00:35:33,214 --> 00:35:35,550
I don't know how I'll survive without money.

507
00:35:35,550 --> 00:35:37,886
I have siblings to take care of,

508
00:35:37,886 --> 00:35:39,610
and I still haven't paid their tuition yet.

509
00:35:39,610 --> 00:35:41,950
My mom needs to see a doctor,

510
00:35:41,950 --> 00:35:43,480
and I need money for that.

511
00:35:43,480 --> 00:35:45,555
I don't have time to understand anyone.

512
00:35:45,555 --> 00:35:48,271
I can't afford to die, even if I wanted to.

513
00:35:48,271 --> 00:35:50,148
So if you want to die, do it somewhere else.

514
00:35:50,148 --> 00:35:51,693
Understood?

515
00:35:52,760 --> 00:35:54,340
Yes.

516
00:35:55,400 --> 00:35:57,210
I'm so sorry.

517
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:13,510
[Laundry service]
Thank you, Tang.

518
00:36:13,510 --> 00:36:14,520
Yes.

519
00:36:18,880 --> 00:36:20,000
Ran.

520
00:36:22,980 --> 00:36:24,420
Hey,

521
00:36:25,330 --> 00:36:27,560
did she get soaked?

522
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:29,356
What did she do?

523
00:36:32,920 --> 00:36:34,620
Wow, I'm so happy

524
00:36:34,620 --> 00:36:36,020
to see you drink it all like this.

525
00:36:36,020 --> 00:36:37,870
Usually, you only take a few sips.

526
00:36:37,870 --> 00:36:39,020
When it's dinnertime,

527
00:36:39,020 --> 00:36:41,560
make sure you eat this much too.

528
00:36:41,560 --> 00:36:42,580
I'm full now, Mom.

529
00:36:42,580 --> 00:36:43,610
This is enough for me.

530
00:36:43,610 --> 00:36:45,420
What?

531
00:36:45,420 --> 00:36:46,670
Come on, Ran.

532
00:36:46,670 --> 00:36:48,780
Love yourself a bit more, won't you?

533
00:36:48,780 --> 00:36:51,790
Don't stress too much about being unemployed.

534
00:36:51,790 --> 00:36:54,850
I sell soy milk and offer laundry services

535
00:36:54,850 --> 00:36:57,750
to earn enough to support the four of us.

536
00:36:57,750 --> 00:37:01,940
Danai is working part-time at a restaurant
to earn his own spending money.

537
00:37:01,940 --> 00:37:04,590
If you keep pushing yourself
and something happens to you,

538
00:37:04,590 --> 00:37:07,680
how could we bear that?

539
00:37:07,680 --> 00:37:10,610
If you can't find a job yet,
then take a break for now.

540
00:37:10,610 --> 00:37:11,730
Do you remember

541
00:37:11,730 --> 00:37:15,540
the last time you had a good night's sleep
and a proper meal?

542
00:37:15,540 --> 00:37:17,640
Because I can't remember that.

543
00:37:18,361 --> 00:37:20,560
But there's still their tuition,

544
00:37:20,560 --> 00:37:23,490
the backup money in case
you need to see a doctor,

545
00:37:23,490 --> 00:37:27,412
- and also--
- Yeah, yeah. Stop. I know that.

546
00:37:27,412 --> 00:37:29,670
You're the one who shouldn't be stressed.

547
00:37:29,670 --> 00:37:33,720
Don't forget you have arrhythmia
and still need to take your medication.

548
00:37:33,720 --> 00:37:36,350
Then don't make me worry.

549
00:37:38,370 --> 00:37:40,680
What about Dao?

550
00:37:40,680 --> 00:37:42,670
She went upstairs to study.

551
00:37:42,670 --> 00:37:45,480
Danai is working at the restaurant.

552
00:37:47,890 --> 00:37:50,860
Mom, don't tell them I got laid off.

553
00:37:52,010 --> 00:37:54,030
I don't want them to worry about our situation.

554
00:37:54,030 --> 00:37:55,630
They might lose focus on their studies.

555
00:37:55,630 --> 00:37:58,030
I'll just tell them

556
00:37:58,030 --> 00:38:00,960
I'm sick and taking some time off.

557
00:38:00,960 --> 00:38:03,260
Yeah, okay.

558
00:38:35,840 --> 00:38:37,380
<i>Yai!</i>

559
00:38:39,680 --> 00:38:41,180
<i>Yai!</i>

560
00:38:52,200 --> 00:38:54,940
<i>Ran, Yai was looking at you.</i>

561
00:39:39,340 --> 00:39:41,800
You know what I'm going
to chew you out for, yes?

562
00:39:42,910 --> 00:39:44,480
I'm not stupid, Mom.

563
00:39:44,480 --> 00:39:46,210
Yeah, genius.

564
00:39:46,210 --> 00:39:49,280
If you're so smart, then don't upset Nana.

565
00:39:49,280 --> 00:39:50,870
What if she breaks the engagement?

566
00:39:50,870 --> 00:39:52,620
What if she pulls out her investment?

567
00:39:52,620 --> 00:39:54,890
How would you handle that?

568
00:39:54,890 --> 00:39:56,170
You idiot.

569
00:39:56,170 --> 00:39:57,190
Goddamn idiot!

570
00:39:57,190 --> 00:39:59,590
I did everything you asked of me.

571
00:39:59,590 --> 00:40:01,840
I already devoted my life to you.

572
00:40:02,680 --> 00:40:04,990
If I asked you for just one thing,
would you give it to me?

573
00:40:04,990 --> 00:40:06,290
What?

574
00:40:06,290 --> 00:40:09,940
I'd rather be an idiot than
have to live off a woman.

575
00:40:19,680 --> 00:40:22,000
Did you hear what he said, Mom?

576
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:23,680
I heard everything.

577
00:40:23,680 --> 00:40:25,750
I just didn't want to show up.

578
00:40:25,750 --> 00:40:28,530
What... What did he mean by that?

579
00:40:28,530 --> 00:40:33,500
It means he wants to prove himself.

580
00:40:33,500 --> 00:40:37,230
If Sahaphet pulls out of
our partnership one day,

581
00:40:37,230 --> 00:40:39,330
he'll never fall.

582
00:40:39,330 --> 00:40:43,900
Because he'll save this TV station
with his own hands.

583
00:40:45,673 --> 00:40:47,983
Do you understand now?

584
00:40:51,160 --> 00:40:52,280
Oh!

585
00:40:52,280 --> 00:40:54,900
That's brilliant!

586
00:40:54,900 --> 00:40:56,280
Oh, gosh.

587
00:40:56,280 --> 00:40:59,700
I n-n-need to write it down,
in case of an interview.

588
00:41:00,880 --> 00:41:03,937
Wait, how am I going to do that?
I don't have a pen.

589
00:41:03,937 --> 00:41:05,680
Anyone here?

590
00:41:05,680 --> 00:41:06,858
Yes? I'm here.

591
00:41:06,858 --> 00:41:09,860
Give me a pen and paper before I forget. Quick.

592
00:41:22,910 --> 00:41:25,370
Do you feel better now?

593
00:41:26,680 --> 00:41:27,860
Yes.

594
00:41:31,480 --> 00:41:34,430
I'll have someone
redecorate your favorite spot.

595
00:41:34,430 --> 00:41:36,000
It'll be stunning.

596
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:38,100
We'll put a chair there

597
00:41:38,100 --> 00:41:40,380
and add a few plants.

598
00:41:40,380 --> 00:41:43,480
Then you'll be able to stargaze
for a long while.

599
00:41:43,480 --> 00:41:45,860
You'll keep stressing yourself out

600
00:41:46,690 --> 00:41:48,820
if you keep doing everything
your mom tells you to.

601
00:41:48,820 --> 00:41:51,490
But she's my mother, Grandma.

602
00:41:51,490 --> 00:41:54,280
I hope you realize it soon.

603
00:41:54,280 --> 00:41:55,560
You're speaking in riddles again.

604
00:41:55,560 --> 00:41:57,730
I don't have the brainpower to figure it out.

605
00:41:57,730 --> 00:41:59,920
Then go have dinner, alright?

606
00:41:59,920 --> 00:42:01,920
No need to think.

607
00:42:01,920 --> 00:42:06,960
Some people they only realize
things when it's too late.

608
00:42:06,960 --> 00:42:08,690
You're doing it again.

609
00:42:10,500 --> 00:42:12,320
Then don't think about it, and go have dinner

610
00:42:12,320 --> 00:42:14,460
before the food gets cold.

611
00:42:20,980 --> 00:42:23,660
It's nice that you're getting
some rest like this, Ran.

612
00:42:23,660 --> 00:42:26,570
This way, we can stargaze
together here more often.

613
00:42:27,900 --> 00:42:30,660
Then who'll pay for your tuition?

614
00:42:31,880 --> 00:42:35,540
I can do part-time work like Danai.

615
00:42:35,540 --> 00:42:37,620
You're just 13 years old.

616
00:42:38,480 --> 00:42:40,570
Focus on your studies,

617
00:42:40,570 --> 00:42:44,500
have fun with your friends,
enjoy being a teenager,

618
00:42:45,700 --> 00:42:47,830
and leave that to me.

619
00:42:47,830 --> 00:42:49,020
What a headache.

620
00:42:49,020 --> 00:42:50,845
Let's relax a little.

621
00:42:51,600 --> 00:42:56,775
I'll sing a song for you,
so listen, alright?

622
00:42:56,775 --> 00:42:58,880
It's your favorite song.

623
00:43:01,100 --> 00:43:05,461
<i>♪ If you're a mountain, then I'll be a forest ♪</i>

624
00:43:05,461 --> 00:43:09,686
<i>♪ Embracing you to keep you warm in my chest ♪</i>

625
00:43:09,686 --> 00:43:13,811
<i>♪ If you're the sky, then I'll be the clouds ♪</i>

626
00:43:13,811 --> 00:43:17,856
<i>♪ Embracing you to keep you company ♪</i>

627
00:43:17,856 --> 00:43:22,296
<i>♪ If you're a car, then I'll be the roads ♪</i>

628
00:43:25,880 --> 00:43:27,380
Are you a high school graduate?

629
00:43:28,700 --> 00:43:29,940
Yes.

630
00:43:32,620 --> 00:43:33,670
Well,

631
00:43:33,670 --> 00:43:35,500
can you smile for me?

632
00:43:50,890 --> 00:43:52,890
What a waste of your beauty, huh?

633
00:44:27,330 --> 00:44:28,770
Hello.

634
00:44:31,770 --> 00:44:34,690
Is this the MJTV station?

635
00:44:36,980 --> 00:44:38,390
Pardon?

636
00:44:39,640 --> 00:44:43,960
Sam can only pair with Luknut.

637
00:44:43,960 --> 00:44:49,729
Sam can only pair with Luknut.

638
00:44:49,729 --> 00:44:52,600
Sam can only pair with Luknut.

639
00:44:52,600 --> 00:44:54,430
[Sam Luknut]
Sam can only pair with Luknut.

640
00:44:54,430 --> 00:44:56,010
Sam can only pair with Luknut.

641
00:44:56,010 --> 00:44:57,830
- Excuse me.
- Sam can only pair with Luknut.

642
00:44:57,830 --> 00:45:02,463
Sam can only pair with Luknut.

643
00:45:02,463 --> 00:45:08,194
Sam can only pair with Luknut.

644
00:45:08,194 --> 00:45:13,580
Sam can only pair with Luknut.

645
00:45:13,580 --> 00:45:19,229
Sam can only pair with Luknut.

646
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:21,370
Let go.

647
00:45:23,280 --> 00:45:25,475
Which way do I have to go?

648
00:45:25,475 --> 00:45:27,585
You really don't remember me?

649
00:45:30,214 --> 00:45:31,689
It's alright.

650
00:45:31,689 --> 00:45:35,419
I'm the one who called you about your sister.

651
00:45:35,419 --> 00:45:38,560
Where is she? Take me to her, please.

652
00:45:38,560 --> 00:45:39,700
Yes.

653
00:45:47,000 --> 00:45:49,650
Your sister is upstairs. Follow me.

654
00:45:49,650 --> 00:45:51,440
[MJTV Broadcasting]

655
00:46:37,047 --> 00:46:39,049
<i>Fire this security team.</i>

656
00:46:39,049 --> 00:46:40,453
<i>Get to the point</i>

657
00:46:40,453 --> 00:46:43,528
<i>before security takes you away
and you lose your chance forever.</i>

658
00:46:43,528 --> 00:46:45,863
<i>I won't allow it!</i>

659
00:46:45,863 --> 00:46:48,185
<i>Dao, did you get to meet the chairman?</i>

660
00:46:48,185 --> 00:46:50,120
<i>I never thought I'd see her again.</i>

661
00:46:50,120 --> 00:46:52,390
<i>What does she want, Auntie?</i>

662
00:46:52,390 --> 00:46:54,210
<i>Meeting like this...</i>

663
00:46:54,210 --> 00:46:56,370
<i>if it isn't destiny, then what is?</i>

664
00:46:56,370 --> 00:46:59,422
<i>Do you have feelings for my sister?
You keep staring at her.</i>

665
00:46:59,422 --> 00:47:00,450
<i>Dao.</i>

666
00:47:00,450 --> 00:47:02,080
<i>Security guard.</i>

667
00:47:02,080 --> 00:47:03,350
<i>What job was it again?</i>

668
00:47:03,350 --> 00:47:05,060
<i>Is Ran at home?</i>
